## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-process IPC with AIDL, runtime plugin loading and verification, media encoding paths, and secure buffer handling under restart and swap scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- Android isolatedProcess, Binder/IPC, AIDL surface
- DexClassLoader plugin loading with signature verification
- MediaCodec hardware acceleration and streaming to UI
- Hot-swapping plugins without service restart
- Encryption of temporary buffers and lifecycle hygiene

## Code Example
```aidl
// ITranscoder.aidl
package com.example transcoder;

interface ITranscoder {
  FrameResult transcodeFrame(in FrameData frame);
  TranscodeStatus getStatus();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test plugin swap safety under low-memory conditions?
- What are fallback behaviors if a plugin fails validation during hot-swap?

## Why This Is Asked
Interviews for advanced Android roles benefit from multi-process isolation and streaming ML workloads. This tests IPC design, security, and performance under strict latency.

## Key Concepts
- android:process and android:isolatedProcess for sandboxing
- AIDL streaming interfaces and Binder optimizations
- on-device ML model loading, versioning, and hot-swapping
- memory/privacy: encrypted buffers, Keystore, secure logging
- latency budgeting and test planning

